WEBVTT

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:13.780
just so stories by Rudyard Kipling copyright black cat publishing

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:28.750
the elephants child part one the elephants child is a

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:35.150
young elephant and he lives in the forest in Africa he's gray and he's got big

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:41.370
ears and his nose is small he's a curious

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:46.510
elephant and he asks a lot of questions one hot

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:51.390
summer day he asks his aunt ostrich why have

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:55.950
you got a lot of feathers his aunt gets angry

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:10.610
and hits him he asks his tall uncle giraffe why have

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:16.590
he asks his big aunt hippopotamus why have you got

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:23.430
red eyes his aunt gets angry and hits him the

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:28.150
elephants child goes to his uncle baboon he asks him

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:33.570
why are bananas good to eat you eat them

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:39.370
every day his uncle gets angry and hits him too

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:44.610
one beautiful day the elephants child goes to the

00:01:44.660 --> 00:01:49.270
other elephants and asks a new question what does the

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:53.730
crocodile have for dinner the other elephants

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:59.530
get angry and say be quiet then they hit the

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:03.610
elephants child when he sees the beautiful

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:09.890
collar collar bird he asks can you help me what

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:20.930
do you want asks the collar collar bird what does

00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:25.070
the green limpop or river and find out says the collar

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:28.950
collar bird the next morning the elephants

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:33.770
child sees some friends and talks to them good morning

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:38.270
my friends says the elephants child I'm

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:42.650
going to the limpop or river I want to find

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:48.890
out what the crocodile has for dinner good luck to you say

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:55.330
his friends thank you he says happily he takes six

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:58.770
bananas and some other fruit and starts walking

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:03.470
one day he sees a python sitting in a tall

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:17.370
tree excuse me python says the elephants child does a

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:21.770
crocodile lives in the green limpop or river what does

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:26.770
he have for dinner asks the elephants child the

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:30.990
python gets angry and hits the elephants child with his

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:35.610
long tail oh dear the elephants child

00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:41.430
thinks everyone is angry with me I must go to

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:47.110
the limpop or river he turns around and slowly goes

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:47.660
away

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:57.710
part two the elephants child arrives at the limpop or

00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:02.810
river he sees a new animal in the big green river

00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:11.110
what a strange animal he thinks what is it excuse

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:32.170
me he asks does a crocodile live here yes little

00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:37.130
please tell me what you have for dinner yes of

00:04:37.180 --> 00:04:44.110
course says the crocodile happily come close to me and I

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:48.930
can tell you the elephants child goes close to the

00:04:48.980 --> 00:04:55.410
crocodile today I'm going to have the elephants child

00:04:55.460 --> 00:05:02.750
for dinner he says laughing he bites the elephants child's

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:07.890
little nose oh my poor nose cries the elephants child

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:12.830
what are you doing the python sees everything and wants

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:16.650
to help the elephants child he quickly goes to him

00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:20.990
and says pull hard the crocodile wants to eat you

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:25.710
and he's very strong the python helps the elephants child

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:31.530
and they pull together the crocodile pulls and the elephants child and

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:36.390
the python pull the elephants child's nose becomes very

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:41.610
long at last the crocodile let's go and he is

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:47.990
very angry the elephants child is free thank you python

00:05:48.040 --> 00:05:54.730
says the elephants child happily you're a good friend your

00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:58.710
nose is very long now says the python looking at it

00:05:58.760 --> 00:06:05.190
oh dear you're right says the elephants child and he

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:11.000
looks at his long nose what can I do with this long nose

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:15.690
the python thinks for a moment and says you can

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:21.110
do a lot of things please tell me says the elephants child

00:06:21.160 --> 00:06:25.390
you can kill flies and you can eat green leaves

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:30.610
from tall trees you can have a cold shower with water from the river

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:34.630
and you can hit other animals your new nose is

00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:41.390
very useful you're right I can do a lot of things with it

00:06:41.440 --> 00:06:46.350
says the elephants child he goes home and shows the

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:50.820
other elephants his new nose look at my new nose

00:06:51.280 --> 00:06:56.650
he says it's very long and useful he tells them

00:06:56.700 --> 00:07:02.880
about all the things he can do with it his friends are surprised and like it a lot

00:07:03.720 --> 00:07:07.750
we want a new nose like yours say his friends

00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:12.160
that's easy says the elephants child

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:18.370
go to the crocodile at Limpapa river he can give

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:23.570
you a long new nose like mine the elephants go

00:07:23.620 --> 00:07:26.370
to the green river and find the crocodile

00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:31.070
soon they all have long new noses and they are

00:07:31.120 --> 00:07:36.580
very happy and this is how the elephant got his trunk

00:07:40.060 --> 00:07:47.470
old man kangaroo the kangaroo is a grey animal with

00:07:47.520 --> 00:07:52.810
four short legs and a long tail he lives in Australia

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:59.110
he likes dancing and he's clever one day at six

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:02.990
o'clock in the morning the kangaroo goes to the little magician

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:08.890
good morning little magician says kangaroo please make me different

00:08:08.940 --> 00:08:11.200
from the other animals what?

00:08:11.980 --> 00:08:16.360
cries the little magician angrily go away kangaroo

00:08:17.620 --> 00:08:22.750
the kangaroo goes away and has breakfast at eight o

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:25.020
'clock he goes to the middle magician

00:08:26.030 --> 00:08:29.750
i want to be different from the other animals says

00:08:29.800 --> 00:08:34.370
the kangaroo and i want to be popular make me

00:08:34.420 --> 00:08:36.150
different and popular

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:41.680
what? cries the middle magician angrily go away

00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:47.400
before lunch the kangaroo goes to the big magician

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:52.890
hello big magician says the kangaroo make me popular and

00:08:52.940 --> 00:08:56.250
different i want the other animals to run after me

00:08:56.300 --> 00:09:02.230
the big magician is having a bath but looks at him and has an idea

00:09:02.280 --> 00:09:07.480
all right kangaroo says the big magician come here dingo

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:15.170
the dingo goes to the big magician what must i do asks the dingo

00:09:15.220 --> 00:09:19.290
do you see that grey animal asks the big magician

00:09:19.340 --> 00:09:26.300
yes i do says the dingo you must run after him says the big magician

00:09:27.280 --> 00:09:30.210
the dingo starts running after the kangaroo

00:09:30.260 --> 00:09:35.930
the two animals run everywhere through the green trees of

00:09:35.980 --> 00:09:38.290
the forest and through the hot desert

00:09:38.340 --> 00:09:42.370
they run up and down the hills and the mountains

00:09:42.420 --> 00:09:47.920
they run through the tall green grass and the short brown grass

00:09:48.760 --> 00:09:53.830
at first the kangaroo likes running fast he thinks it's

00:09:53.880 --> 00:09:54.550
great fun

00:09:54.600 --> 00:10:01.830
but after a few hours he gets tired i can't stop running now

00:10:01.880 --> 00:10:05.730
thinks the kangaroo the dingo wants to catch me

00:10:05.780 --> 00:10:10.650
the dingo likes running fast but he is tired too

00:10:10.700 --> 00:10:12.870
i can't stop running now

00:10:12.920 --> 00:10:15.940
thinks the dingo but i'm hungry

00:10:16.840 --> 00:10:20.730
the kangaroo and the dingo run all over australia

00:10:20.780 --> 00:10:24.990
when they get to the wolgong river there is no bridge

00:10:25.040 --> 00:10:27.820
the kangaroo stops running

00:10:28.680 --> 00:10:30.820
how can i cross the river?

00:10:31.680 --> 00:10:32.650
thinks the kangaroo

00:10:32.700 --> 00:10:36.540
there is no bridge so i must hop across

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:41.310
he hops across the river and gets to the other side

00:10:41.360 --> 00:10:42.840
that's easy

00:10:43.360 --> 00:10:47.050
he thinks it's easy to hop and i like it

00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:51.410
he pulls up his front legs and uses his tail

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:52.260
to help him

00:10:53.140 --> 00:10:55.560
then he hops again and again

00:10:56.260 --> 00:10:57.670
i love hopping

00:10:57.720 --> 00:10:58.760
he thinks

00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:04.260
so he hops through the deserts of australia and the dingo follows him

00:11:05.120 --> 00:11:06.700
when is he going to stop?

00:11:07.260 --> 00:11:08.350
thinks the dingo

00:11:08.400 --> 00:11:10.480
i'm very hungry

00:11:11.200 --> 00:11:16.780
at five o'clock in the afternoon the kangaroo and the dingo see the big magician

00:11:17.660 --> 00:11:20.800
he is sitting in the river having another bath

00:11:21.560 --> 00:11:24.080
they stop and sit by the river

00:11:26.100 --> 00:11:27.880
i'm very tired

00:11:28.220 --> 00:11:29.400
says the kangaroo

00:11:30.320 --> 00:11:33.390
and i'm very hungry says the dingo

00:11:33.440 --> 00:11:35.270
why don't you thank the dingo?

00:11:35.320 --> 00:11:38.440
the big magician asks the kangaroo

00:11:39.090 --> 00:11:41.270
thank him says the kangaroo

00:11:41.320 --> 00:11:42.220
why?

00:11:42.920 --> 00:11:43.860
you want to be different?

00:11:44.540 --> 00:11:45.730
says the big magician

00:11:45.780 --> 00:11:48.880
no you're different look at your legs and your long tail

00:11:49.880 --> 00:11:51.890
but my long legs are funny

00:11:51.940 --> 00:11:53.650
says the kangaroo

00:11:53.700 --> 00:11:55.650
looking at his legs

00:11:55.700 --> 00:11:58.010
do you want the dingo to run after you until

00:11:58.060 --> 00:11:58.320
midnight?

00:11:59.100 --> 00:12:00.310
asks the big magician

00:12:00.360 --> 00:12:03.590
no, no says the kangaroo

00:12:03.640 --> 00:12:06.410
my legs and long tail are fine

00:12:06.460 --> 00:12:07.410
i like them

00:12:07.460 --> 00:12:11.320
but now i'm very hungry i am too

00:12:11.800 --> 00:12:12.720
says the dingo

00:12:13.820 --> 00:12:15.900
what can i have for dinner?

00:12:17.060 --> 00:12:18.270
ask me tomorrow

00:12:18.320 --> 00:12:20.340
says the big magician

00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:24.050
so the kangaroo and the dingo

00:12:24.100 --> 00:12:27.650
are tired and hungry in the middle of australia

00:12:27.700 --> 00:12:30.140
they look at each other

00:12:30.920 --> 00:12:32.990
all of this is your fault

00:12:33.040 --> 00:12:34.290
says the dingo

00:12:34.340 --> 00:12:37.110
now it's not says kangaroo

00:12:37.160 --> 00:12:38.490
it's your fault

00:12:38.540 --> 00:12:39.710
you're wrong

00:12:39.760 --> 00:12:41.030
says the dingo

00:12:41.080 --> 00:12:42.430
it's your fault

00:12:42.480 --> 00:12:44.390
and at midnight

00:12:44.440 --> 00:12:46.860
they are still arguing

00:12:50.740 --> 00:12:53.120
the animals of australia

00:12:54.620 --> 00:12:56.530
australia has a lot of animals

00:12:56.580 --> 00:12:57.730
that you can't find

00:12:57.780 --> 00:12:59.380
in other places in the world

00:13:00.520 --> 00:13:02.230
let's have a look at some of them

00:13:02.280 --> 00:13:03.860
the kangaroo

00:13:04.920 --> 00:13:06.010
the kangaroo

00:13:06.060 --> 00:13:07.630
is probably the most popular

00:13:07.680 --> 00:13:09.000
animal of australia

00:13:09.540 --> 00:13:11.490
the kangaroo is a marsupial

00:13:11.540 --> 00:13:14.840
that means that it carries its young in a special pouch

00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:18.150
a baby kangaroo is called a joey

00:13:18.200 --> 00:13:20.290
when a joey is born

00:13:20.340 --> 00:13:24.180
it is very small only about two centimeters long

00:13:24.840 --> 00:13:26.910
it lives in its mother's pouch

00:13:26.960 --> 00:13:29.320
for nine months before leaving it

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:31.230
the kangaroo

00:13:31.280 --> 00:13:32.830
is a herbivore

00:13:32.880 --> 00:13:34.890
it eats only grass

00:13:34.940 --> 00:13:37.440
and plants and does not eat meat

00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:40.410
it can grow to two meters

00:13:40.460 --> 00:13:42.740
and weigh around 90 kilograms

00:13:43.560 --> 00:13:45.780
it moves about by hopping

00:13:46.540 --> 00:13:48.340
some kangaroos are red

00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:49.960
and some are grey

00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:52.920
they live in all parts of australia

00:13:54.920 --> 00:13:56.020
the koala

00:13:57.040 --> 00:14:00.300
the koala is often called the koala bear

00:14:00.780 --> 00:14:02.390
because it looks like a small bear

00:14:02.440 --> 00:14:04.280
but it is not a bear

00:14:04.780 --> 00:14:05.980
it is a marsupial

00:14:06.820 --> 00:14:07.970
it lives in trees

00:14:08.020 --> 00:14:10.360
and does not like staying on the ground

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:12.870
it eats leaves and fruit

00:14:12.920 --> 00:14:16.160
the koala sleeps most of the day in trees

00:14:16.660 --> 00:14:18.160
and usually eats at night

00:14:18.920 --> 00:14:20.850
it lives in eastern and southern

00:14:20.900 --> 00:14:22.500
australia near the sea

00:14:23.440 --> 00:14:24.650
the emu

00:14:24.700 --> 00:14:26.550
the emu

00:14:26.600 --> 00:14:28.770
is a very big bird in australia

00:14:28.820 --> 00:14:32.990
it is about two meters tall it does not fly

00:14:33.040 --> 00:14:35.010
but it can run very fast

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:37.550
around 50 kilometers an hour

00:14:37.600 --> 00:14:40.830
it lives in all areas of australia

00:14:40.880 --> 00:14:42.670
but it doesn't like forests

00:14:42.720 --> 00:14:44.630
it eats plants

00:14:44.680 --> 00:14:45.940
and insects

00:14:48.500 --> 00:14:49.670
the platypus

00:14:49.720 --> 00:14:54.150
the platypus lives in small rivers in eastern australia

00:14:55.020 --> 00:14:56.990
and is an excellent swimmer

00:14:57.040 --> 00:14:59.490
it has a very strange nose

00:14:59.540 --> 00:15:02.120
this looks like a duck's mouth

00:15:02.960 --> 00:15:05.650
it can also live in and out of water

00:15:05.700 --> 00:15:08.050
it sleeps during the day

00:15:08.100 --> 00:15:09.400
and moves at night

00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:12.700
it eats small animals and insects

00:15:13.380 --> 00:15:15.400
it is about the size of a cat

00:15:19.560 --> 00:15:21.680
how the leopard got his spots

00:15:23.080 --> 00:15:24.200
part one

00:15:26.700 --> 00:15:29.890
all the animals of the hot African savanna

00:15:29.940 --> 00:15:33.040
are a dark yellow or light brown color

00:15:34.240 --> 00:15:36.890
they are the same color as the grass and trees

00:15:36.940 --> 00:15:37.640
around them

00:15:38.620 --> 00:15:41.550
it's difficult to see the dark yellow giraffe

00:15:41.600 --> 00:15:43.390
and the light brown zebra

00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:45.090
and the leopard

00:15:45.140 --> 00:15:46.950
is very difficult to see

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:51.660
because he is exactly the same color as the savanna

00:15:52.700 --> 00:15:56.890
the leopard often hunts giraffes and zebras with a young man

00:15:56.940 --> 00:15:59.980
they are both very good hunters

00:16:01.120 --> 00:16:02.890
all the giraffes and zebras

00:16:02.940 --> 00:16:04.280
are afraid of them

00:16:05.460 --> 00:16:07.190
I'm afraid of the leopard

00:16:07.240 --> 00:16:09.090
because I can't see him

00:16:09.140 --> 00:16:11.830
and he always surprises me

00:16:11.880 --> 00:16:13.320
says the zebra

00:16:13.820 --> 00:16:14.430
you're right

00:16:14.480 --> 00:16:15.970
says the giraffe

00:16:16.020 --> 00:16:17.630
I'm afraid of him too

00:16:17.680 --> 00:16:21.020
but I'm also very afraid of the man

00:16:21.880 --> 00:16:24.370
we're always in danger here

00:16:24.420 --> 00:16:25.750
says the zebra

00:16:25.800 --> 00:16:28.130
why don't we go somewhere else

00:16:28.180 --> 00:16:29.020
yes

00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:30.930
let's go away

00:16:30.980 --> 00:16:32.390
says the giraffe

00:16:32.440 --> 00:16:33.590
follow me

00:16:33.640 --> 00:16:36.470
so the giraffe and the zebra

00:16:36.520 --> 00:16:38.170
go to a big forest

00:16:38.220 --> 00:16:42.330
this is a lovely forest with beautiful colors

00:16:42.380 --> 00:16:44.530
says the giraffe happily

00:16:44.580 --> 00:16:48.830
yes everything is green, brown or black

00:16:48.880 --> 00:16:51.130
and it's not hot here

00:16:51.180 --> 00:16:52.530
says the zebra

00:16:52.580 --> 00:16:58.470
I like it there are a lot of tall green trees in the forest

00:16:58.520 --> 00:17:00.570
the trees and plants

00:17:00.620 --> 00:17:02.490
make strange shadows

00:17:02.540 --> 00:17:04.890
they fall on the animals

00:17:04.940 --> 00:17:06.770
and they don't go away

00:17:06.820 --> 00:17:08.570
look at me

00:17:08.620 --> 00:17:10.200
says the giraffe

00:17:10.820 --> 00:17:12.950
I've got some patches on my body

00:17:13.000 --> 00:17:16.140
yes you have says the zebra

00:17:16.580 --> 00:17:17.740
they are beautiful

00:17:18.460 --> 00:17:22.470
and you've got some wonderful stripes on your body

00:17:22.520 --> 00:17:24.140
says the giraffe

00:17:24.820 --> 00:17:26.770
the zebra looks at his body

00:17:26.820 --> 00:17:28.200
and sees the stripes

00:17:28.820 --> 00:17:34.150
he likes them and he's happy now we can hide from the leopard

00:17:34.200 --> 00:17:35.600
says the giraffe

00:17:36.100 --> 00:17:38.790
he can smell us and he can hear us

00:17:38.840 --> 00:17:41.380
but he can't see us

00:17:42.140 --> 00:17:46.400
the zebra and the giraffe are happy and safe in the big forest

00:17:47.740 --> 00:17:49.890
the leopard and the man go hunting

00:17:49.940 --> 00:17:53.580
but they can't find the zebra and the giraffe

00:17:54.200 --> 00:17:56.540
where are the zebra and the giraffe?

00:17:56.920 --> 00:17:57.830
asks the man

00:17:57.880 --> 00:17:59.890
I can smell them

00:17:59.940 --> 00:18:01.690
and I can hear them

00:18:01.740 --> 00:18:03.610
but I can't see them

00:18:03.660 --> 00:18:05.020
says the leopard

00:18:05.880 --> 00:18:08.430
they go and ask a clever baboon

00:18:08.480 --> 00:18:09.680
called Bhavian

00:18:10.720 --> 00:18:13.260
where are the zebra and the giraffe?

00:18:13.760 --> 00:18:14.710
asks the leopard

00:18:14.760 --> 00:18:17.540
we can't find them and we're hungry

00:18:18.340 --> 00:18:21.200
you must go through the big green forest

00:18:21.740 --> 00:18:23.160
said Bhavian

00:18:23.740 --> 00:18:25.350
you can find them there

00:18:25.400 --> 00:18:27.570
and you can look for spots too

00:18:27.620 --> 00:18:28.530
spots

00:18:28.580 --> 00:18:30.430
asks the leopard

00:18:30.480 --> 00:18:31.700
yes spots

00:18:32.500 --> 00:18:33.510
says Bhavian

00:18:33.560 --> 00:18:35.370
I don't understand

00:18:35.420 --> 00:18:36.950
says the leopard

00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:39.090
when you're in the green forest

00:18:39.140 --> 00:18:40.810
look for spots

00:18:40.860 --> 00:18:42.730
says Bhavian

00:18:42.780 --> 00:18:46.130
the leopard and the man go to the forest

00:18:46.180 --> 00:18:48.350
but they can't find the animals

00:18:48.400 --> 00:18:50.390
what a strange place

00:18:50.440 --> 00:18:51.750
says the leopard

00:18:51.800 --> 00:18:56.190
yes it's dark but it's full of spots of light

00:18:56.240 --> 00:18:57.480
says the man

00:18:58.240 --> 00:19:01.460
are these the spots Bhavian talks about?

00:19:01.920 --> 00:19:02.910
asks the leopard

00:19:02.960 --> 00:19:03.570
perhaps

00:19:03.620 --> 00:19:05.330
says the man

00:19:05.380 --> 00:19:08.210
I can smell a giraffe

00:19:08.260 --> 00:19:11.010
and I can hear a giraffe

00:19:11.060 --> 00:19:12.090
says the man

00:19:12.140 --> 00:19:16.310
but I can't see it and I can smell a zebra

00:19:16.360 --> 00:19:18.750
and I can hear a zebra

00:19:18.800 --> 00:19:20.110
says the leopard

00:19:20.160 --> 00:19:24.890
but I can't see it they look around the forest

00:19:24.940 --> 00:19:27.220
why can't we see them?

00:19:27.600 --> 00:19:28.490
asks the man

00:19:28.540 --> 00:19:30.580
that's a good question

00:19:31.200 --> 00:19:32.580
says the leopard

00:19:36.240 --> 00:19:37.760
part two

00:19:39.260 --> 00:19:42.290
I know the animals are here somewhere

00:19:42.340 --> 00:19:43.790
says the leopard

00:19:43.840 --> 00:19:46.040
but I can't see them

00:19:46.820 --> 00:19:48.650
let's wait until the night

00:19:48.700 --> 00:19:50.150
all right

00:19:50.200 --> 00:19:51.460
says the man

00:19:52.200 --> 00:19:54.120
they sit down and wait

00:19:54.980 --> 00:19:59.030
when it is dark they hear and smell the zebra

00:19:59.080 --> 00:19:59.810
and the giraffe

00:19:59.860 --> 00:20:02.950
the man catches the giraffe

00:20:03.000 --> 00:20:05.150
ah now you're mine

00:20:05.200 --> 00:20:06.450
he says happily

00:20:06.500 --> 00:20:09.030
and the leopard catches the zebra

00:20:09.080 --> 00:20:10.870
and now you're mine

00:20:10.920 --> 00:20:11.930
he shouts

00:20:11.980 --> 00:20:13.500
looking at the zebra

00:20:14.200 --> 00:20:16.730
but there's something strange about these animals

00:20:16.780 --> 00:20:18.590
you're right

00:20:18.640 --> 00:20:19.860
says the man

00:20:20.640 --> 00:20:22.880
let's wait until morning and see

00:20:23.880 --> 00:20:25.230
the next morning

00:20:25.280 --> 00:20:26.590
the leopard and the man

00:20:26.640 --> 00:20:28.650
look at the two animals carefully

00:20:28.700 --> 00:20:31.740
what's this says the leopard

00:20:32.440 --> 00:20:33.920
a zebra with stripes

00:20:34.640 --> 00:20:38.020
and what's this says the man

00:20:38.280 --> 00:20:40.540
a giraffe with patches

00:20:41.640 --> 00:20:43.290
the leopard and the man

00:20:43.340 --> 00:20:44.490
are very surprised

00:20:44.540 --> 00:20:46.970
the giraffe and the zebra

00:20:47.020 --> 00:20:47.660
laugh

00:20:48.940 --> 00:20:50.640
why are you different?

00:20:51.340 --> 00:20:52.320
asks the leopard

00:20:52.820 --> 00:20:54.790
looking at the zebra and the giraffe

00:20:54.840 --> 00:20:56.690
please let us go

00:20:56.740 --> 00:20:58.550
and we can show you our trick

00:20:58.600 --> 00:20:59.940
says the giraffe

00:21:00.700 --> 00:21:02.400
yes show us

00:21:03.020 --> 00:21:04.800
say the leopard and the man

00:21:05.700 --> 00:21:07.450
the giraffe and the zebra

00:21:07.500 --> 00:21:09.660
go under the tall green trees

00:21:10.820 --> 00:21:13.050
suddenly the leopard and the man

00:21:13.100 --> 00:21:14.310
can't see them anymore

00:21:14.360 --> 00:21:16.580
where are you?

00:21:16.960 --> 00:21:17.890
asks the man

00:21:17.940 --> 00:21:20.640
the giraffe and the zebra laugh

00:21:23.260 --> 00:21:25.490
I can hear you laugh

00:21:25.540 --> 00:21:28.460
but I can't see you says the leopard

00:21:29.960 --> 00:21:31.530
laughs the giraffe

00:21:31.580 --> 00:21:33.500
where's your breakfast now?

00:21:34.480 --> 00:21:35.990
the leopard and the man

00:21:36.040 --> 00:21:41.500
don't know where they are we're here under the tall trees

00:21:42.200 --> 00:21:43.530
says the zebra

00:21:43.580 --> 00:21:45.410
but it's almost impossible

00:21:45.460 --> 00:21:47.650
to see us because we look like

00:21:47.700 --> 00:21:49.170
the shadows of the forest

00:21:49.220 --> 00:21:50.310
you're right

00:21:50.360 --> 00:21:51.660
says the leopard

00:21:52.400 --> 00:21:54.510
that's a very good trick

00:21:54.560 --> 00:21:55.820
says the man

00:21:56.540 --> 00:21:58.790
I think I need spots too

00:21:58.840 --> 00:22:00.100
says the leopard

00:22:01.380 --> 00:22:03.190
that's what bavian says

00:22:03.240 --> 00:22:04.560
and he's clever

00:22:05.460 --> 00:22:06.750
it's a good idea

00:22:06.800 --> 00:22:07.870
says the man

00:22:07.920 --> 00:22:10.640
it's more difficult to see you with spots

00:22:11.840 --> 00:22:14.090
the leopard goes into the forest

00:22:14.140 --> 00:22:16.570
and its shadows fall on him

00:22:16.620 --> 00:22:19.950
now he has dark spots on his body

00:22:20.000 --> 00:22:21.780
and they don't go away

00:22:22.780 --> 00:22:25.690
you've got some lovely dark spots

00:22:25.740 --> 00:22:27.570
all over your body

00:22:27.620 --> 00:22:29.260
says the man

00:22:29.840 --> 00:22:30.810
I like them

00:22:30.860 --> 00:22:32.030
says the leopard

00:22:32.080 --> 00:22:34.390
now I can hide in the forest

00:22:34.440 --> 00:22:36.430
like the giraffe and the zebra

00:22:36.480 --> 00:22:38.770
yes says the man

00:22:38.820 --> 00:22:42.190
now no one can find you in the forest

00:22:42.240 --> 00:22:45.660
I'm very happy says the leopard

00:22:46.440 --> 00:22:47.620
and I'm hungry

00:22:48.440 --> 00:22:49.460
let's go hunting

00:22:50.160 --> 00:22:51.910
yes good idea

00:22:51.960 --> 00:22:53.200
says the man

