00:24:57.520 --> 00:24:59.520
how the whale got his throat

00:25:00.920 --> 00:25:03.170
the whale is a big animal

00:25:03.220 --> 00:25:04.790
and he lives in the sea

00:25:04.840 --> 00:25:07.210
he is always hungry and eats

00:25:07.260 --> 00:25:09.460
many different fish and sea animals

00:25:10.080 --> 00:25:11.420
he doesn't have a throat

00:25:11.980 --> 00:25:14.070
and this means he can eat very big things

00:25:14.120 --> 00:25:16.240
as well as very small things

00:25:17.100 --> 00:25:18.510
a very small fish

00:25:18.560 --> 00:25:19.940
called the little fish

00:25:20.320 --> 00:25:21.620
also lives in the sea

00:25:22.300 --> 00:25:23.280
he is clever

00:25:24.120 --> 00:25:27.550
the whale is eating all the fish in the sea

00:25:27.600 --> 00:25:29.070
the little fish thinks

00:25:29.120 --> 00:25:30.800
I'm afraid

00:25:31.520 --> 00:25:33.500
I don't want him to eat me

00:25:34.340 --> 00:25:36.760
I must hide behind his ear

00:25:37.560 --> 00:25:40.770
but suddenly the whale stands up on his big tail

00:25:40.820 --> 00:25:42.580
and sees the little fish

00:25:43.500 --> 00:25:47.580
I'm hungry says the whale in a loud voice

00:25:48.660 --> 00:25:49.680
what's this?

00:25:50.840 --> 00:25:51.980
a little fish

00:25:52.860 --> 00:25:54.370
hello great whale

00:25:54.420 --> 00:25:56.330
says the little fish

00:25:56.380 --> 00:25:58.800
do you like eating man?

00:25:59.440 --> 00:26:01.280
I don't know

00:26:01.740 --> 00:26:02.570
says the whale

00:26:02.620 --> 00:26:04.300
looking at the little fish

00:26:04.860 --> 00:26:07.940
I prefer dolphins or sharks

00:26:08.900 --> 00:26:11.010
what is man like?

00:26:11.060 --> 00:26:17.050
oh man is very good says the clever little fish

00:26:17.100 --> 00:26:18.200
really?

00:26:19.120 --> 00:26:20.180
says the whale

00:26:20.980 --> 00:26:21.320
yes

00:26:22.020 --> 00:26:22.950
says the little fish

00:26:23.000 --> 00:26:24.460
believe me

00:26:25.700 --> 00:26:28.070
can you find a man for me

00:26:28.120 --> 00:26:29.630
asks the whale

00:26:29.680 --> 00:26:33.640
of course I can says the little fish

00:26:34.380 --> 00:26:36.530
you must swim to the north

00:26:36.580 --> 00:26:38.810
and in the middle of the sea

00:26:38.860 --> 00:26:41.560
there is a young sailor on a raft

00:26:42.260 --> 00:26:44.390
he's wearing blue trousers

00:26:44.440 --> 00:26:45.740
and braces

00:26:47.020 --> 00:26:48.710
good let's go

00:26:48.760 --> 00:26:50.080
says the whale

00:26:50.860 --> 00:26:52.510
the whale and the little fish

00:26:52.560 --> 00:26:54.140
swim across the sea

00:26:54.800 --> 00:26:56.650
soon the whale sees the sailor

00:26:56.700 --> 00:26:57.720
sitting on a raft

00:26:59.660 --> 00:27:02.140
good I'm very hungry

00:27:02.820 --> 00:27:03.510
says the whale

00:27:03.560 --> 00:27:05.450
he opens his big mouth

00:27:05.500 --> 00:27:07.150
and eats the young sailor

00:27:07.200 --> 00:27:08.240
and the raft

00:27:10.900 --> 00:27:12.510
says the whale

00:27:12.560 --> 00:27:17.970
man is very good the sailor and his raft

00:27:18.020 --> 00:27:20.130
are inside the whale's stomach

00:27:20.180 --> 00:27:22.480
what's happening to me?

00:27:22.840 --> 00:27:23.700
thinks the sailor

00:27:24.240 --> 00:27:25.050
he is afraid

00:27:25.100 --> 00:27:27.000
where am I?

00:27:28.040 --> 00:27:30.100
it's warm and dark in here

00:27:30.820 --> 00:27:33.970
oh no I'm inside a whale

00:27:34.020 --> 00:27:36.120
what can I do?

00:27:36.920 --> 00:27:38.590
the sailor is very clever

00:27:38.640 --> 00:27:41.750
and looks around he starts thinking

00:27:41.800 --> 00:27:44.770
this whale can't eat me

00:27:44.820 --> 00:27:46.250
he says angrily

00:27:46.300 --> 00:27:48.290
he starts jumping

00:27:48.340 --> 00:27:50.030
kicking and dancing

00:27:50.080 --> 00:27:51.630
inside the whale's stomach

00:27:51.680 --> 00:27:54.010
the whale is very unhappy

00:27:54.060 --> 00:27:55.570
and feels ill

00:27:55.620 --> 00:27:59.720
I've got a terrible stomach ache

00:28:00.820 --> 00:28:02.610
says the unhappy whale

00:28:02.660 --> 00:28:04.870
I'm sorry whale

00:28:04.920 --> 00:28:06.540
says the little fish

00:28:07.400 --> 00:28:09.660
what's the sailor doing?

00:28:10.380 --> 00:28:11.250
asks the whale

00:28:11.300 --> 00:28:14.560
do you know little fish?

00:28:15.440 --> 00:28:16.870
I don't know

00:28:16.920 --> 00:28:18.190
says the little fish

00:28:18.240 --> 00:28:20.350
the sailor continues

00:28:20.400 --> 00:28:22.510
jumping kicking and dancing

00:28:22.560 --> 00:28:23.930
inside the whale's stomach

00:28:23.980 --> 00:28:25.800
oh says the whale

00:28:26.450 --> 00:28:27.720
I feel sick

00:28:28.650 --> 00:28:30.310
I'm going to ask the sailor

00:28:30.360 --> 00:28:32.740
to come out says the little fish

00:28:33.360 --> 00:28:34.640
thank you

00:28:35.280 --> 00:28:36.560
that's a good idea

00:28:37.200 --> 00:28:38.020
says the whale

00:28:38.860 --> 00:28:40.820
please come out

00:28:41.360 --> 00:28:42.580
cries the little fish

00:28:43.360 --> 00:28:44.160
what?

00:28:45.300 --> 00:28:46.030
answers the sailor

00:28:46.080 --> 00:28:50.390
the whale's got a terrible stomach ache

00:28:50.440 --> 00:28:51.700
says the little fish

00:28:52.360 --> 00:28:54.680
please come out right now

00:28:55.360 --> 00:29:00.150
no I'm not coming out says the sailor angrily

00:29:00.200 --> 00:29:05.560
you must take me home to England first all right

00:29:07.020 --> 00:29:08.500
says the poor whale

00:29:09.400 --> 00:29:11.480
I can take you home

00:29:12.640 --> 00:29:14.510
the whale and the little fish

00:29:14.560 --> 00:29:15.990
start swimming fast

00:29:16.040 --> 00:29:18.350
they swim across the sea to England

00:29:18.400 --> 00:29:21.170
while the whale and the little fish swim

00:29:21.220 --> 00:29:23.270
the sailor breaks up the raft

00:29:23.320 --> 00:29:25.230
and ties the pieces together

00:29:25.280 --> 00:29:25.990
with his braces

00:29:26.040 --> 00:29:28.790
when they get to the beach in England

00:29:28.840 --> 00:29:31.570
the sailor has a big surprise

00:29:31.620 --> 00:29:32.500
for the whale

00:29:34.080 --> 00:29:36.750
whale open your big mouth

00:29:36.800 --> 00:29:38.550
says the sailor

00:29:38.600 --> 00:29:40.480
I want to get out

00:29:41.420 --> 00:29:43.390
the whale opens his mouth

00:29:43.440 --> 00:29:48.710
and the sailor walks out but he leaves his raft in the whale's mouth

00:29:48.760 --> 00:29:52.310
now my raft is your throat

00:29:52.360 --> 00:29:55.230
and you can never eat men again

00:29:55.280 --> 00:29:56.560
says the sailor

00:29:56.910 --> 00:29:57.910
with this raft

00:29:57.960 --> 00:30:00.850
you can only eat very small fish

00:30:00.900 --> 00:30:02.160
what?

00:30:02.840 --> 00:30:05.280
only very small fish

00:30:06.190 --> 00:30:07.720
says the whale angrily

00:30:08.010 --> 00:30:10.650
I don't want this in my throat

00:30:10.700 --> 00:30:16.650
the whale coughs and coughs

00:30:16.700 --> 00:30:18.400
but the raft doesn't move

00:30:18.950 --> 00:30:22.270
he is very sad and slowly swims away

00:30:22.320 --> 00:30:24.310
the sailor is on the beach

00:30:24.360 --> 00:30:26.380
and watches the whale swim away

00:30:27.320 --> 00:30:28.630
goodbye whale

00:30:28.680 --> 00:30:30.390
says the sailor happily

00:30:30.440 --> 00:30:32.760
now you can't eat men anymore

00:30:34.620 --> 00:30:36.310
men aren't nice

00:30:36.360 --> 00:30:39.070
and they give me a stomach ache

00:30:39.120 --> 00:30:40.100
says the whale

00:30:40.860 --> 00:30:44.020
small fish are much better

00:30:48.180 --> 00:30:48.860
whales

00:30:50.120 --> 00:30:52.180
what do you know about whales?

00:30:53.300 --> 00:30:54.760
here are some interesting facts

00:30:55.940 --> 00:30:57.530
whales live in the sea

00:30:57.580 --> 00:30:58.990
but they are not fish

00:30:59.040 --> 00:31:00.050
they are mammals

00:31:00.100 --> 00:31:02.150
they need air to live

00:31:02.200 --> 00:31:04.970
they must come up to the top of the water

00:31:05.020 --> 00:31:05.410
often

00:31:05.460 --> 00:31:06.610
to get air

00:31:06.660 --> 00:31:11.500
they breathe air in and out through the blowhole on their back

00:31:12.120 --> 00:31:13.630
when whales sleep

00:31:13.680 --> 00:31:15.790
they stay on the top of the water

00:31:15.840 --> 00:31:19.490
the biggest whale is the blue whale

00:31:19.540 --> 00:31:24.320
it is around 30 meters long and weighs about 200 tons

00:31:25.840 --> 00:31:31.280
whales swim by moving their tails up and down and by using their flippers

00:31:31.840 --> 00:31:37.190
their flippers help them to turn around whales make a lot of noise

00:31:37.240 --> 00:31:39.300
because they talk to each other

00:31:39.840 --> 00:31:43.460
their underwater sounds can travel very far

00:31:45.840 --> 00:31:47.650
whales usually live in groups

00:31:47.700 --> 00:31:50.960
a baby whale is called a calf

00:31:51.840 --> 00:31:53.840
plural, calves

00:31:55.760 --> 00:32:00.990
whales move from one place to another during the warm summer months

00:32:01.040 --> 00:32:04.300
they eat a lot because they get ready for the winter

00:32:04.840 --> 00:32:07.630
in the autumn they start moving south

00:32:07.680 --> 00:32:08.910
to warm places

00:32:08.960 --> 00:32:11.940
and in the spring they move north

00:32:12.650 --> 00:32:17.170
the killer whale is a very popular and dangerous whale

00:32:17.220 --> 00:32:21.910
here is some information about it the killer whale

00:32:21.960 --> 00:32:23.610
name

00:32:23.660 --> 00:32:25.090
orca

00:32:25.140 --> 00:32:26.850
or killer whale

00:32:26.900 --> 00:32:28.410
color

00:32:28.460 --> 00:32:29.730
black

00:32:29.780 --> 00:32:30.510
and white

00:32:30.560 --> 00:32:32.090
size

00:32:32.140 --> 00:32:35.010
around 8 meters for males

00:32:35.060 --> 00:32:37.000
and 7 meters for females

00:32:38.120 --> 00:32:38.970
lives

00:32:39.020 --> 00:32:41.110
in all major oceans

00:32:41.160 --> 00:32:45.590
from the Arctic areas of Alaska, Canada, Scandinavia

00:32:45.640 --> 00:32:48.460
and Russia to the warm oceans in the south

00:32:49.160 --> 00:32:52.540
they usually live in groups of around 40 whales

00:32:53.320 --> 00:32:57.200
the killer whale can live for 30 to 50 years

00:32:58.860 --> 00:33:01.540
eats, fish and other sea animals

00:33:02.040 --> 00:33:04.060
a very dangerous predator

00:33:08.140 --> 00:33:10.380
how the camel got his hump

00:33:11.300 --> 00:33:15.330
the horse, the dog and the ox work for the farmer

00:33:15.380 --> 00:33:20.700
but the camel does not he has a long neck and long legs

00:33:21.360 --> 00:33:23.190
he lives alone in the desert

00:33:23.240 --> 00:33:25.090
and doesn't want to work

00:33:25.140 --> 00:33:27.290
he eats and sleeps

00:33:27.340 --> 00:33:29.970
and when someone speaks to him

00:33:30.020 --> 00:33:30.730
he says

00:33:30.780 --> 00:33:31.610
hump

00:33:31.660 --> 00:33:36.330
on Monday morning the horse goes to see the camel

00:33:36.380 --> 00:33:38.650
camel says the horse

00:33:38.700 --> 00:33:41.310
come and work like all the other animals

00:33:41.360 --> 00:33:44.970
I carry men on my back and work hard all day

00:33:45.020 --> 00:33:45.720
hump

00:33:46.500 --> 00:33:49.400
says the camel and the horse goes away

00:33:50.300 --> 00:33:53.730
on Tuesday morning the dog goes to see the camel

00:33:53.780 --> 00:33:56.090
camel says the dog

00:33:56.140 --> 00:33:58.310
come and work like all the other animals

00:33:58.360 --> 00:34:00.740
I guard the farmer's house

00:34:01.200 --> 00:34:03.610
I work hard day and night

00:34:03.660 --> 00:34:06.130
hump says the camel

00:34:06.180 --> 00:34:08.160
and the dog goes away

00:34:09.180 --> 00:34:12.930
on Wednesday the big ox goes to see the camel

00:34:12.980 --> 00:34:15.890
camel says the big ox

00:34:15.940 --> 00:34:17.760
come and work for the farmer

00:34:18.360 --> 00:34:20.580
I work hard in the country all day

00:34:21.840 --> 00:34:23.700
hump says the camel

00:34:24.160 --> 00:34:25.800
and the ox goes away

00:34:26.840 --> 00:34:30.070
the animals go and tell the farmer about the lazy

00:34:30.120 --> 00:34:30.470
camel

00:34:30.520 --> 00:34:33.240
the camel is very lazy

00:34:33.560 --> 00:34:34.310
says the horse

00:34:34.360 --> 00:34:36.000
he doesn't want to work

00:34:36.580 --> 00:34:37.330
says the ox

00:34:37.380 --> 00:34:39.670
he just eats and sleeps

00:34:39.720 --> 00:34:40.610
and says

00:34:40.660 --> 00:34:43.220
hump says the dog

00:34:43.800 --> 00:34:46.550
the farmer thinks for a moment and then says

00:34:46.600 --> 00:34:49.260
you three must work more than

00:34:49.720 --> 00:34:50.060
what?

00:34:50.820 --> 00:34:51.850
the animals say

00:34:51.900 --> 00:34:58.890
but we don't want to work more you must work more because the camel doesn't want to work

00:34:58.940 --> 00:35:00.500
says the farmer

00:35:01.060 --> 00:35:06.540
the horse the ox and the dog are very angry and they start talking

00:35:07.300 --> 00:35:09.930
the camel walks by and listens to them

00:35:09.980 --> 00:35:13.150
hump says the camel

00:35:13.200 --> 00:35:15.000
and goes away laughing

00:35:15.960 --> 00:35:19.650
the animals don't know what to do we need help

00:35:19.700 --> 00:35:20.750
says the horse

00:35:20.800 --> 00:35:24.090
yes says the dog sadly

00:35:24.140 --> 00:35:26.300
but who can help us?

00:35:27.160 --> 00:35:31.000
suddenly the desert magician arrives on a big cloud

00:35:31.800 --> 00:35:34.570
he is a great magician and lives in the desert

00:35:34.620 --> 00:35:37.160
he is everyone's friend

00:35:37.800 --> 00:35:38.160
hello?

00:35:38.840 --> 00:35:39.280
he says

00:35:39.790 --> 00:35:41.260
what are you talking about?

00:35:42.120 --> 00:35:43.060
why are you angry?

00:35:43.940 --> 00:35:45.280
oh desert magician

00:35:45.670 --> 00:35:46.450
says the horse

00:35:46.500 --> 00:35:48.250
we have a big problem

00:35:48.300 --> 00:35:50.140
what's your problem?

00:35:50.800 --> 00:35:51.950
asks the desert magician

00:35:52.000 --> 00:35:57.690
tell me about it the camel in the desert doesn't want to work

00:35:57.740 --> 00:35:58.830
says the horse

00:35:58.880 --> 00:36:01.680
why doesn't he want to work?

00:36:02.220 --> 00:36:03.910
asks the desert magician

00:36:03.960 --> 00:36:05.680
he is lazy

00:36:06.300 --> 00:36:07.070
says the ox

00:36:07.120 --> 00:36:08.030
yes

00:36:08.080 --> 00:36:09.490
says the horse

00:36:09.540 --> 00:36:10.930
very lazy

00:36:10.980 --> 00:36:13.730
and we must do more work

00:36:13.780 --> 00:36:14.950
says the dog

00:36:15.000 --> 00:36:19.460
we already work hard all day long says the ox

00:36:20.000 --> 00:36:22.300
what does the camel say?

00:36:22.840 --> 00:36:24.490
asks the desert magician

00:36:24.540 --> 00:36:26.530
he always says

00:36:26.580 --> 00:36:27.470
hump

00:36:27.520 --> 00:36:29.280
says the horse

00:36:29.980 --> 00:36:32.360
i must go and talk to the camel

00:36:33.000 --> 00:36:34.560
says the desert magician

00:36:35.480 --> 00:36:38.070
the desert magician's magic cloud

00:36:38.120 --> 00:36:39.510
carries him to the desert

00:36:39.560 --> 00:36:41.390
and he sees the camel

00:36:41.440 --> 00:36:44.380
he is standing near a pool of water

00:36:45.140 --> 00:36:47.840
why don't you want to work camel?

00:36:48.520 --> 00:36:50.080
asks the desert magician

00:36:50.980 --> 00:36:51.700
humph

00:36:52.500 --> 00:36:53.570
says the camel

00:36:53.620 --> 00:36:55.810
looking at the pool of water

00:36:55.860 --> 00:37:01.270
the other animals must work more because you don't work

00:37:01.320 --> 00:37:03.260
says the desert magician

00:37:04.080 --> 00:37:04.750
humph

00:37:04.800 --> 00:37:06.380
says the camel

00:37:07.200 --> 00:37:08.380
don't say

00:37:09.200 --> 00:37:09.870
humph

00:37:09.920 --> 00:37:11.450
says the desert magician

00:37:11.500 --> 00:37:14.250
you must start working

00:37:14.300 --> 00:37:17.110
the camel looks at himself

00:37:17.160 --> 00:37:18.590
in the pool of water

00:37:18.640 --> 00:37:21.930
i'm a great magician

00:37:21.980 --> 00:37:23.810
thinks the desert magician

00:37:23.860 --> 00:37:26.600
what magic can i do?

00:37:27.560 --> 00:37:30.260
the camel must work

00:37:30.920 --> 00:37:35.450
the desert magician sits down and thinks about something magic

00:37:35.500 --> 00:37:40.100
suddenly the camel has a big hump on his back

00:37:40.700 --> 00:37:42.530
he looks in the pool of water

00:37:42.580 --> 00:37:45.160
and sees it he is very surprised

00:37:46.200 --> 00:37:47.620
what's that on my back?

00:37:48.320 --> 00:37:49.980
he asks the desert magician

00:37:50.800 --> 00:37:51.580
it's your

00:37:52.440 --> 00:37:53.000
humph

00:37:53.640 --> 00:37:55.100
says the desert magician

00:37:55.940 --> 00:38:00.090
i don't like it and i don't want it says the camel

00:38:00.140 --> 00:38:00.980
angrily

00:38:01.880 --> 00:38:04.730
how can i work with this hump on my back

00:38:04.780 --> 00:38:08.510
now you can work more than the other animals

00:38:08.560 --> 00:38:10.350
says the desert magician

00:38:10.400 --> 00:38:11.910
with your hump

00:38:11.960 --> 00:38:14.790
you don't need to eat or drink

00:38:14.840 --> 00:38:16.310
for three days

00:38:16.360 --> 00:38:17.200
what?

00:38:17.900 --> 00:38:19.140
says the camel angrily

00:38:19.780 --> 00:38:21.690
i don't want to work

00:38:21.740 --> 00:38:24.230
now be quiet

00:38:24.280 --> 00:38:27.050
and start working

00:38:27.100 --> 00:38:29.530
says the desert magician

00:38:29.580 --> 00:38:32.670
the camel walks away slowly

00:38:32.720 --> 00:38:34.680
and joins the other animals

00:38:35.720 --> 00:38:37.510
when the other animals see him

00:38:37.560 --> 00:38:39.960
they laugh and laugh

00:38:40.720 --> 00:38:42.150
on that day

00:38:42.200 --> 00:38:44.100
the camel starts working

00:38:44.560 --> 00:38:46.920
but he still isn't friendly
